🧠 Mental Illness Prediction using Machine Learning
🚀 Overview

This project builds an end-to-end Machine Learning system to predict mental health conditions based on survey data. It covers the complete pipeline from data preprocessing to model deployment using Flask.

🎯 Problem Statement

Mental health issues are often underdiagnosed. This project aims to build a predictive system that can identify individuals at risk based on behavioral and demographic inputs.

📊 Dataset
Survey-based dataset (Kaggle)
Features include:
Age, Gender
Work environment
Mental health indicators
Target variable:
Mental Illness (Yes/No)
🧠 Machine Learning Pipeline
1. Data Preprocessing
Handling missing values
Encoding categorical variables
2. EDA
Distribution analysis
Class imbalance detection (~97% vs 3%)
3. Handling Imbalance
Applied SMOTE only on training data
Avoided data leakage
4. Model Building
Random Forest
XGBoost (final model)
5. Model Evaluation
Precision, Recall, F1-score
ROC-AUC
📈 Results
Improved recall for minority class using SMOTE
XGBoost achieved best performance
Balanced precision-recall tradeoff
🌐 Deployment
Flask-based web app
Real-time prediction from user input
⚙️ How to Run

pip install -r requirements.txt
python app.py

🚨 Challenges Faced
Highly imbalanced dataset
Mixed data types (YES/NO, categorical values)
Avoiding overfitting and data leakage
